From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:24:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 115/120] Bold and italic in Markdown files (Ctrl+B, Ctrl+I)

Ctrl+B and Ctrl+I in a Markdown file wrap the selection in ** or *, or
remove the markers when it has them already (just inside or just outside
the selection). Without a selection they act on the word at the cursor,
elsewhere they insert an empty pair with the cursor in the middle. Bold
and italic share the star: ***x*** is both, and toggling one leaves the
other. A selection over several lines wraps each line's text on its
own, after block markers such as "- " or "## ". Lines in fenced code
blocks and text in code spans are left alone. One undo step per use.

The Edit menu lists Bold and Italic with their shortcuts, disabled
outside Markdown files and in the Preview view, where the keys do
nothing. The "/" menu gets inline items: Bold, Italic, Strikethrough
and Inline code insert the markers around a selected "text"; Bold and
Italic show their shortcut as the hint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

